{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505138-how-much-rage-can-you-spend-per-turn-w-20","id":1505138,"title":"How much rage can you spend per turn W 20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-11T14:11:35-08:00","id":1505138,"title":"How much rage can you spend per turn W 20?","content":"Surely it must say so in the book somewhere but I guess I overlooked it. Is it one point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T14:20:27-08:00","id":1505139,"title":"","content":"Revised had it at no more than half your permanent rating per turn. You're also soft-capped in how many actions you can get, as more than the lower of Dex or Wits (only Dex in a frenzy) increases the difficulty of each action by 3.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's the same limit in W20. See page 266, &quot;Spending Rage&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-11-2023, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T22:29:59-08:00","id":1505160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505138-how-much-rage-can-you-spend-per-turn-w-20?p=1505139#post1505139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revised had it at no more than half your permanent rating per turn. You're also soft-capped in how many actions you can get, as more than the lower of Dex or Wits (only Dex in a frenzy) increases the difficulty of each action by 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, this cap was one of the reasons one two many of my characters prefered Hispo over Crinos in a fight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T22:44:20-08:00","id":1505161,"title":"","content":"Generally, the math is on Hispo's side. Crinos only becomes preferable after factoring in the &quot;hands, less likely to get dosed with something via bite, has a fetish weapon&quot; factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T06:02:47-07:00","id":1505171,"title":"","content":"I've had a simple houserule to help with that - as long as you're doing rip and tear stuff you're fine with using Strength as your attack roll base. If you want finesse (i.e. not hitting the flesh armor or the toxic oozing wounds) you use dex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T09:59:48-07:00","id":1505176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505138-how-much-rage-can-you-spend-per-turn-w-20?p=1505171#post1505171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had a simple houserule to help with that - as long as you're doing rip and tear stuff you're fine with using Strength as your attack roll base. If you want finesse (i.e. not hitting the flesh armor or the toxic oozing wounds) you use dex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also one of my rule, V5 also tell to use strength for brawl attack. You still make the damage roll by using strength <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T10:13:34-07:00","id":1505177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505138-how-much-rage-can-you-spend-per-turn-w-20?p=1505176#post1505176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also one of my rule, V5 also tell to use strength for brawl attack. You still make the damage roll by using strength <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. It makes combat faster and scarier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T14:59:07-07:00","id":1505196,"title":"","content":"I would caution about some of the knockout effects it can have. A lot of powers in the books are very generous to Strength in fashions that can make it very powerful to do that house rule if you're not thinking about adjusting other things as they come up. Pre-V20 VtM had the Potence Grapple issue for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T15:44:16-07:00","id":1505200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1505138-how-much-rage-can-you-spend-per-turn-w-20?p=1505196#post1505196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would caution about some of the knockout effects it can have. A lot of powers in the books are very generous to Strength in fashions that can make it very powerful to do that house rule if you're not thinking about adjusting other things as they come up. Pre-V20 VtM had the Potence Grapple issue for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. You're bound to end up fine tuning things as you go along. For me it's been working for almost 2 decades now., though. As for Potence I've always treated in a way that it only added to damage and leaping distance, the rest it wouldn't be applicable on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T16:31:39-07:00","id":1505206,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying don't do it. The CofD has been doing it just fine for about that amount of time now.<br /> <br /> Esp. with WtA's rather disorganized powers (the giant Gift lists, the way different Fera have different form bonuses and Rage boosts, etc) means it's something to keep in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-13T12:29:54-07:00","id":1505263,"title":"","content":"Personnaly i play it like in v5: one roll and a damage bonus added to your result (werewolf claws +2 damage, bite +1 and use the v5 rules for weaponery bonus). Soak is always full and when a pc or npc has a lot of stamina, armor, or both they must use dex instead of strength to target a weak point or use specials moves to weaken their opponent (tear their armor appart, attack from behind. We got rid of damage and soak roll, wich make combat deadlier and faster.<br /> <br /> We've got rid of damage and soaking roll since almost 2 years, now. After few adjustments and a houserule for rolling importants amount of dice (more than 10) and our game work now pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T01:55:56-07:00","id":1505295,"title":"","content":"I play with Dex having a slight nerf - your additional sux are halved for the purposes of figuring out damage dice.<br /> <br /> For instance RAW if you roll 9 successes on an attack, you roll +8 damage dice; which is HUGE. This means Dex is far more important than Strength. A good roll, backed up by good Dex, difficulty modifications, boosts to your attacking stat, seriously outweighs your raw strength.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the houserule I play with halves the overflow. So 9 successes, that's 8/2 = 4. +4 dice - significant, perhaps doubling the pool even, but not drowning out Strength entirely.<br /> <br /> With this houserule I've seen Strength matter a LOT more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}